.TH "C3L" "1" "2026-11-01"
.P
.SH NAME
.P
\fBc3l\fR - reproducible dependencies for C3 projects, on top of \fBc3c fetch\fR.\&
.P
.SH SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBc3l\fR [\fB--registry\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB--dry-run\fR] [\fB--frozen\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.P
.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
\fBc3c fetch\fR installs libraries but records no version, verifies no checksum and
cannot update or remove.\& \fBc3l\fR adds a lockfile, \fIc3l.\&lock\fR, checksum
verification with rollback, and update, outdated, remove and sync.\& Libraries are
kept as \fI.\&c3l\fR zip files in the first entry of \fIdependency-search-paths\fR.\& Run
\fBc3l\fR in the project root.\&
.P
.SH OPTIONS
.P
Options may appear before or after the command.\&
.P
\fB--registry\fR \fIURL\fR, \fB--registry=\fR\fIURL\fR
.RS 4
Use this registry for the command.\& Overrides \fBC3L_REGISTRY\fR and the registry
recorded in \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& Only matters for registry libraries and for \fBsearch\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--dry-run\fR
.RS 4
Only print what \fBupdate\fR would change.\& Has no effect on other commands.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--frozen\fR
.RS 4
For \fBsync\fR, meant for CI.\& Fail if \fIproject.\&json\fR and \fIc3l.\&lock\fR list different
libraries, restore only what the lockfile says, and never write the lockfile.\&
Has no effect on other commands.\&
.P
.RE
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Print the usage text.\&
.P
.RE
\fB-v\fR, \fB--version\fR
.RS 4
Print the version.\&
.P
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.P
\fBinit\fR [\fIname\fR]
.RS 4
Create \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& With \fIname\fR and outside a project, run \fBc3c init\fR first.\&
.P
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fInamespace/name\fR[@\fIversion\fR]
.RS 4
Install a library from the registry with \fBc3c fetch\fR, compare the SHA-256 of the
download with the registry'\&s checksum, write the lock line.\& A mismatch or any
failure restores the previous library file and \fIproject.\&json\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fIgit-url\fR[@\fIref\fR]
.RS 4
Install from a git repository.\& \fIref\fR is a tag, a branch, \fBHEAD\fR, or a full
40-character commit hash; it can also be given as a separate argument.\& Without
a \fIref\fR the highest semantic version tag is used, or HEAD if there are none.\&
The ref is resolved to a commit, which is what the lockfile pins.\& \fBoutdated\fR
and \fBupdate\fR follow the tip of \fBHEAD\fR and of branches; tags and commits stay
put.\& In scp-style URLs (\fIgit@host:path\fR) the \fB@\fR only starts a ref after the
last \fB/\fR.\& The library is built with \fBgit archive\fR, so no \fI.\&git\fR is included.\& The lockfile
records a hash of the library'\&s \fBcontents\fR (a git tree id), not of the zip bytes,
so it does not depend on the compression, timestamps or git version of the
machine that wrote the archive.\& \fBverify\fR and \fBsync\fR compare contents the same
way.\& This needs \fBgit\fR and \fBunzip\fR.\& The repository needs a \fImanifest.\&json\fR at its root.\&
.P
.RE
\fBremove\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Delete the library file, its \fIdependencies\fR entry and its lock line.\&
.P
.RE
\fBlist\fR
.RS 4
Show every locked library with its state: \fIok\fR, \fImodified\fR, \fImissing\fR,
\fIunpacked\fR, and \fIuntracked\fR for libraries in \fIproject.\&json\fR not in the lockfile.\&
.P
.RE
\fBverify\fR
.RS 4
Check installed files against the lockfile.\& Exit status 1 on any difference.\&
.P
.RE
\fBoutdated\fR
.RS 4
Show locked libraries for which the registry (or git) has a higher version.\&
.P
.RE
\fBupdate\fR [\fIname\fR[@\fIref\fR] .\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Update to the newest version, one library at a time, with rollback.\& With
\fIname\fR@\fIref\fR switch that library to an explicit version instead: a registry
version, or for git libraries a tag, branch, \fBHEAD\fR or full commit hash (for
example \fBc3l update lib@HEAD\fR moves a tag-locked library to HEAD).\& With
\fB--dry-run\fR only print what would change.\&
.P
.RE
\fBsync\fR
.RS 4
Make the project match \fIc3l.\&lock\fR: reinstall missing or modified libraries at the
locked version and verify against the locked checksum or commit.\& With
\fB--frozen\fR fail instead if \fIproject.\&json\fR and the lockfile list different
libraries, and never write the lockfile.\&
.P
.RE
\fBsearch\fR \fItext\fR | \fBtag:\fR\fIname\fR
.RS 4
Search the registry (the \fI/search\fR endpoint, else \fBc3c fetch-list\fR).\&
.P
.RE
\fBinfo\fR \fInamespace/name\fR
.RS 4
Run \fBc3c fetch-info\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBmigrate\fR
.RS 4
Convert a c3l 0.\&x \fI.\&c3l.\&deps\fR file into \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\&
.P
.RE
.SH LOCKFILE
.P
Tab separated, one library per line, sorted by name:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
# c3l\&.lock v1
@registry	https://www\&.c3pkg\&.eu
box2d	registry	jecokef902/box2d	1\&.0\&.0	sha256:4945\&.\&.\&.	sha256:4945\&.\&.\&.
hex	git	https://github\&.com/konimarti/hex\&.c3l	v0\&.1\&.1	commit:3fa9\&.\&.\&.	tree:9c1e\&.\&.\&.
.fi
.RE
.P
Columns: name, kind (\fIregistry\fR or \fIgit\fR), source, version, pin (checksum or
commit), SHA-256 of the installed file (registry) or git tree id of its contents (git).\&
.P
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.P
\fIC3L_REGISTRY\fR
.RS 4
Registry base URL.\& Overridden by \fB--registry\fR, overrides the lockfile.\&
Default: https://www.\&c3pkg.\&eu
.P
.RE
\fIC3C\fR
.RS 4
The c3c executable.\& It needs \fBfetch\fR support (0.\&8.\&6 or a nightly).\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_LOCK\fR
.RS 4
Lockfile name.\& Default: \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fIDEBUGC3L\fR
.RS 4
Trace all shell statements.\&
.P
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.P
